url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21649753"
license: "CC-BY-4.0"
abstract: >-
  PQID-Bench is a frozen, self-contained, validation-aware benchmark and
  evidence suite for quantum-program generation. It includes materialized
  514/66/154 train, validation, and test JSONL splits, so use does not require
  reconstruction from the parent PQID dataset. Over its 21-model by 154-prompt
  primary matrix, 2,950 of 3,234 outputs execute in Python, 2,944 are OpenQASM
  3 assembly admissible, and 1,703 recover the frozen reference signature. Its
  38.37-point Assembly-Structure Gap retains 99.52% of the 38.56-point
  Execution-Structure Gap. The separately versioned pqid-bench Python package
  supports verification, numerical reporting, interactive exploration,
  live-model evaluation, and isolated replay without changing the frozen
  evidence.
references:
